      "statusChangeNewStatus": "tracked",
      "value": "LOD0 is not disabled on any quality setting. The \"Maximum LOD Level\" setting is \"0\" for all quality settings. The only change to LOD settings between quality levels is the LOD Bias which ranges from 1.0 to 2.0 between Low and Ultra.\nUltra: 2.0\nHigh: 2.0\nMedium: 1.5\nLow: 1.0\nThis LOD Bias range was already possible using the built-in Unity settings pop-up that was available by holding Shift while starting the client. Users could select between VRHigh, VRLow, and DesktopLow. VRHigh used an LOD Bias of 2.0 while VRLow and DesktopLow used an LOD Bias of 1.0.\nUnity has removed the built-in settings pop-up in Unity 2019 so instead the quality settings have to be available through a VRChat menu option.\nThe new SDK will populate your project's quality settings to match the VRChat client's quality settings so you can see exactly what settings are used for each quality level by opening the project quality settings from Edit->Project Settings->Quality.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
