      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5fa30b66b36d4b12af626dc8|full_name}: Thank you for your detailed answer TCL, I appreciate it. I assume it's only the LOD bias then that can mess with the carefully tweaked LOD ranges for those setups, so the camera is not close enough anymore with a LOD bias of 1.0 while the setup was done/tested for the LOD bias 2.0 only. It would be great if we could do a LOD bias override for the different settings, maybe similar to how we can set walking speed or jump power. I edited my canny to reflect this more accurate and removed the maximum LOD confusion.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
