  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-07-30T18:05:59.661Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat introduced graphics settings in the beta client now, which modifies the LOD bias, resulting in LOD0 not being active when it should.\nThis is breaking some scripts in our world, because the Update() loop checks for LOD0 being rendered to know that the player is close and the object is in sight before running code.\nToggling script logic via LOD renderer (specifically LOD0) is a common way how optimization in UDON is done right now, which is also from the official Unity tutorial https://learn.unity.com/tutorial/fixing-performance-problems\nVRChat cannot argue that we should use area toggles everywhere instead, since those still have their own issues which makes them unusable in some cases https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/colliders-that-are-not-on-the-mirrorreflection-layer-will-stop-the-hand-raycasts\nTo solve this, we should be able to define our own graphics settings overrides, which would solve the LOD bias issue that we now need to account for. At least the LOD bias should be optionally defineable for a world.",
